{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"About Vedabbha: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja48'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 48 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Atthakāmavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Wanting to Help </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Vedabbajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>About Vedabbha: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Anupāyena yo atthaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Who wishes to profit by inappropriate means </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Icchati so vihaññati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is tormented. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Cetā haniṁsu vedabbaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Cetans who killed Vedabbha </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sabbe te byasanamajjhagūti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>all fell into ruin. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Vedabbajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
